Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their potential usage, and conditions  
• "LANGUAGES"."repo_name": repository identifier to join with commits.  
• "LANGUAGES"."language": detect JavaScript; first inspect typical values, later filter with ILIKE '%javascript%'.  
• "SAMPLE_COMMITS"."repo_name": repository identifier for counting commits.  
• "SAMPLE_COMMITS"."commit": every row represents one commit; COUNT(*) gives commit totals.  
Conditions that will be useful  
• "LANGUAGES"."language" ILIKE '%javascript%'  –– approximate match for JavaScript.  
• GROUP BY "SAMPLE_COMMITS"."repo_name"  –– aggregate commits per repository.  
• ORDER BY commit_count DESC LIMIT 2  –– keep top two repositories by commit total.

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final Snowflake SQL queries (20‑row cap each).  
Every column name is enclosed in double quotes and fully qualified.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at raw language strings to understand the formatting used in the LANGUAGES table.
SELECT "language"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: View repositories whose language field contains the word “javascript” (any case).
SELECT "repo_name",
       "language"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE "language" ILIKE '%javascript%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Count how many repositories advertise JavaScript somewhere in the language column.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "js_repo_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE "language" ILIKE '%javascript%';
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Inspect a few commit rows so we know what the commit column looks like.
SELECT "repo_name",
       "commit",
       "subject"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Determine commit counts for a handful of repositories (no language filter yet).
SELECT "repo_name",
       COUNT(*) AS "commit_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"
GROUP BY "repo_name"
ORDER BY "commit_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Commit counts only for repos whose language field contains “javascript”.
SELECT c."repo_name",
       COUNT(*) AS "commit_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"   c
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"        l
  ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%javascript%'
GROUP BY c."repo_name"
ORDER BY "commit_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Verify that each repo in the join above is unique inside the LANGUAGES table
-- (sometimes the same repo can have multiple language lines).
SELECT l."repo_name",
       COUNT(*) AS "language_rows"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%javascript%'
GROUP BY l."repo_name"
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: When multiple language rows exist for a repo, pick the first one (arbitrary) 
-- and keep filtering by JavaScript.
WITH ranked_lang AS (
    SELECT l."repo_name",
           l."language",
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY l."repo_name" ORDER BY l."repo_name") AS rn
    FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
    WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%javascript%'
)
SELECT *
FROM ranked_lang
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Join that de‑duplicated language list to commit data for accurate commit counts.
WITH ranked_lang AS (
    SELECT l."repo_name",
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY l."repo_name" ORDER BY l."repo_name") AS rn
    FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
    WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%javascript%'
),
js_repos AS (
    SELECT "repo_name"
    FROM ranked_lang
    WHERE rn = 1
)
SELECT c."repo_name",
       COUNT(*) AS "commit_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS" c
JOIN js_repos j
  ON c."repo_name" = j."repo_name"
GROUP BY c."repo_name"
ORDER BY "commit_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Final query – choose the top two JavaScript repositories with the highest commit counts.
WITH ranked_lang AS (
    SELECT l."repo_name",
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY l."repo_name" ORDER BY l."repo_name") AS rn
    FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
    WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%javascript%'
),
js_repos AS (
    SELECT "repo_name"
    FROM ranked_lang
    WHERE rn = 1
),
commits_per_repo AS (
    SELECT c."repo_name",
           COUNT(*) AS "commit_cnt"
    FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS" c
    JOIN js_repos j
      ON c."repo_name" = j."repo_name"
    GROUP BY c."repo_name"
)
SELECT "repo_name",
       "commit_cnt"
FROM commits_per_repo
ORDER BY "commit_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 2;
```
